# November 19, 2026: Ballston Spa village, Malta, Crescent, Milton, Day and two Saratoga Springs buildings, drawn at
# random by tools/choose.py --state ny (region sar). Ballston Spa had only three places (the Sans Souci block, Brookside
# and the Union Mill); Malta, Crescent and Day had none of these. Standing buildings mostly: two churches and a post office
# in Ballston Spa, the National Bottle Museum, the Verbeck House, the Wiggins-Collamer House (now a shop), the Noxon Bank
# at Crescent, Bethesda Episcopal Church and the Bryan house in Saratoga Springs, and two odd survivors known from markers
# only: the Rose Hill stone water tower in Milton and the WPA-built old town hall at Day Center (a lead in notes/sar_pgzb.md).
# Sources were opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); HMdb marker pages (tools/page.py); the
# Episcopal Diocese of Albany's page for Christ Church; the New York State Military Museum's armory page; Bethesda's own
# parish history and home page; the First Baptist Church's history article in Saratoga TODAY; the National Bottle Museum's
# home page; Finishing Touches' own page and a 2020 Saratoga Business Journal article for the Collamer house.
