  'Bethesda was incorporated in 1830 and first met in an old spring house given by Dr. John Clarke. The present church on Washington Street was begun in 1842 from plans adapted from Richard Upjohn\'s and finished in 1844, widened in 1860 by moving out the side walls, and consecrated in 1866 once the lot was paid for. The tower on the west front was added in 1887 in memory of Rockwell Putnam, with four bells.',
  'The parish\'s timeline lists stained glass given in 1860, a chancel window and brass eagle lectern given by Spencer Trask in 1887, a marble altar, brass altar rail, reredos and marble font of the same year, marble columns of 1898, and a Casavant organ of 1967. Open for services; interior otherwise not checked.',
